    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3846" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arverni</span></b> , ōrum,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρβερνοί</span>, Plut.;
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρουερνοί</span>, Strabo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of Gaul</i>,
				<i>in the present</i> Auvergne, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G.
				1, 31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 1,
			427</span></i>; cf. Mann. Gall. p. 130.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arvernus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Arvernian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arvernum genus (vini),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 1, 3, § 18</span></i>
			.</div>
